  "reading": {
    "headline": "CoreML cuts median RTF from 2.0417 to 1.5061 (-26.2%).",
    "shape": "The gain is concentrated in utterances up to ~10 s (-26% to -37%). The 23 s paragraph improved by only 3%, so this does not help long-form narration.",
    "still_above_realtime": "Even at the improved figure the tier remains slower than realtime, so this reduces dead air between sentences rather than eliminating it. Kokoro (0.64 in-pipeline) is still the only engine measured that keeps up.",
    "cold_start_cost": "Cold ready rose from 8124.2 ms to 17933.6 ms (+9809 ms), consistent with first-load ANE compilation. Whether macOS caches that across process restarts was not tested."
  },
  "evidence_limits": [
    "BINARY PROVENANCE IS THE BIG ONE. build/qwen3-tts-worker dates from 2026-08-16 while the engine source sits at 22277bc6f087 with src/tts_transformer.cpp uncommitted (`22277bc-dirty`). The baseline here measures 2.042 where F7 recorded 1.33 for the same tier and byte-identical GGUF, so these ABSOLUTE numbers are not comparable to F7. Both legs used the identical binary, so the RATIO is internally valid; the absolute level is not. Rebuilding the engine was deliberately not done: the tree carries another session's uncommitted work.",
    "n=3 per fixture in a single session; per-run RTF swings up to +/-25% (F1 coreml: 1.506 / 1.804 / 1.400), so individual fixture deltas have wide error bars. The consistent direction across four of five fixtures is the signal, not any single figure.",
    "max_abs_diff 0.230287 against the torch reference means CoreML logits are close but not identical, and sampling is stochastic (temperature 0.9, top-k 50). Audio durations differed between legs; RTF normalizes for that, wall time does not.",
    "English output quality was NOT judged. No ear check was performed, and a numerically-close predictor can still change prosody.",
    "0.6b only. The 1.7b export was not attempted: its HF weights are not on this machine.",
    "Apple Silicon only; the CoreML path does not exist on other platforms."
  ],
  "durable_value": "Records that the acceleration path the engine already supports is simply absent from the shipped package, and quantifies what it is worth. A packaging change (ship the mlpackage, or generate it at install) is the follow-up, and needs its own workitem with a quality check.",
  "next": [
    "Rebuild the worker from a clean engine pin and re-run both legs, to get numbers comparable to F7's 1.33 baseline.",
    "Ear-check English output against the ggml predictor before shipping.",
    "Export and measure the 1.7b tier.",
    "Confirm whether the ANE compile is cached across restarts, since +9.8 s of cold start matters at session start."
  ]
}
